    "completion": "Orientation keeps its separate non-graded completion policy from AGENTS.md: a bare chosen interest label starts the tailored follow-up rather than certifying subject mastery; closure follows the prescribed meaningful follow-up or explicit wish to leave and separate learner agreement. The same stable existing orientation ID is reused, so already completed orientation is not a newly authored competence.",
    "consumerP": "All four actual consumer cases, both expectation bodies, coverage rules, variation axes, statuses and E1/G1/ai_candidate authority are retained. The two numeric finite-menu examples still give A then D, with the stated ordinal individual rankings and bounded information/attention assumptions. No autonomous model-construction, universal utility, bias diagnosis or whole-source approval is gained from this edge.",
    "atomicityMemoryVisualization": "The current consumer remains one conceptual explanatory atom and keeps atomic=true/no_memory_needed decisions. Whole current A/M review paths and bodies, 66 card records, 34 visibility scopes, visualization/QA pointers and all actual consumer resource links are exact. No new memorization or image performance is asserted.",
    "source": "The actual Berlin household-theory source scope previously inspected remains unchanged. The 125-row current tuple changes only the consumer requires value, whole-goal hash and P input fingerprint. All 124 other rows and all 208 partial mapping edges/strengths are exact. Source-aspect derivation, candidate status and course/coverage limits are retained; pointer freshness does not add a source approval."
